# What NOT to upload to AppSail.
#
# The CLI packs a deploy by opening a read stream for EVERY file in the build
# path at the same time. With node_modules included that is tens of thousands
# of simultaneous handles, and Windows answers EMFILE: too many open files.
# The deploy then dies, and the CLI's own error handler hits the same limit
# reading its config — producing an unhandled-rejection loop that wrote a
# 12.9 GB catalyst-debug.log before it was stopped.
#
# Catalyst installs dependencies and runs `npm run build` on its side, so none
# of this needs to travel.
#
# Both directory and glob forms are listed deliberately: the packer matches
# with minimatch against paths that use the platform separator, so on Windows a
# pattern written only as `node_modules/**/*` can fail to match
# `node_modules\next\...`. The bare directory entry prunes the walk instead.

node_modules
node_modules/**
node_modules/**/*

.next
.next/**
.next/**/*

.git
.git/**
.git/**/*

.claude
.claude/**
.claude/**/*

# Secrets belong in the AppSail service's environment variables, never inside
# the uploaded package.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.local.backup-*

*.log
catalyst-debug.log
